title: mos65xx-python
message: >-
  If you use this work, or the states it was settled against, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gustavo
    family-names: Franco
    alias: gufranco
repository-code: https://github.com/gufranco/mos65xx-python
url: https://github.com/gufranco/mos65xx-python
abstract: >-
  A model of the MOS 6502 family and the WDC 65C816, the processors inside the machines
  that defined eight-bit and sixteen-bit home computing. Every documented instruction,
  addressing mode, cycle and bus line is settled against recorded states and against the
  manufacturers' own data sheets rather than against its author's confidence, and nothing
  in it starts from a clean machine, because silicon powers up holding whatever it holds.
keywords:
  - emulation
  - 6502
  - 65816
  - mos-technology
  - wdc
  - hardware-model
  - conformance
  - cycle-accurate
